      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-num">4</div>
        <h2>Your daily workflow</h2>
      </div>

      <p>Here's a practical breakdown of what a typical day looks like using Kasper at the front desk.</p>

      <div class="step-list">
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="step-bubble">AM</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <strong>Morning Huddle</strong>
            <span>Open Kasper and review the Morning Huddle dashboard. It shows today's production goal, scheduled production by provider, confirmed vs. unconfirmed appointments, and any open flags from yesterday — unpaid balances, incomplete forms, unresolved tasks.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="step-bubble">1</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <strong>Review insurance verification</strong>
            <span>Kasper runs eligibility checks automatically before appointments. Check the dashboard for any red or yellow flags — coverage issues, inactive insurance, waiting periods — and resolve them before the patient arrives so checkout has no surprises.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="step-bubble">2</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <strong>Check form submissions</strong>
            <span>Forms are sent to patients automatically when they schedule. Confirm today's patients have submitted. If not, send a quick text from Kasper with a new link — they can fill it out on their phone while they wait.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="step-bubble">3</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <strong>Handle calls &amp; texts</strong>
            <span>Incoming calls trigger a screen pop with the patient's full Open Dental context — next appointment, last visit, balance, hygiene due date, and unscheduled treatment. After the call, Kasper's AI writes a summary to their chart automatically. Respond to texts from the Kasper messaging panel.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="step-bubble">4</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <strong>Monitor the intraday dashboard</strong>
            <span>Keep the dashboard open all day. Patient cards are color-coded — act on any flag before the patient moves to checkout. The dashboard also shows how long each patient has been waiting and their total time in office, so you can spot bottlenecks early.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="step-bubble">5</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <strong>Fill cancellations with Opportunity Finder</strong>
            <span>When a cancellation creates a gap, open Opportunity Finder immediately. Select the treatment type that fits the slot — Kasper shows you a ranked list of patients to call or text with one click. Don't leave the chair empty.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="step-bubble">6</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <strong>Process checkout &amp; payments</strong>
            <span>Collect via terminal, saved card, or send a text-to-pay link. KasperPay posts the payment to Open Dental immediately. If the patient needs a payment plan, set it up directly in Kasper — automated charges and ledger posting are handled from there.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="step-bubble">PM</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <strong>End-of-day sweep</strong>
            <span>Review the Revenue Leakage Protector for unallocated payments, pending claims, and open balances. Check for failed auto-payments from the payment transactions report and send text-to-pay links to those patients. Close out any open tasks before logging off.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

