        <div class="section-num">5</div>
        <h2>Common questions</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Do I need to update Open Dental separately after using Kasper?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">No. Kasper has a two-way real-time sync with Open Dental. Appointments, forms, payments, call summaries, and insurance verification data all flow automatically between the two systems. Nothing needs to be entered twice.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">What happens if a patient doesn't fill out their forms before arriving?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">You can send a new form link directly from Kasper. The patient fills it out on their phone or on an iPad in the waiting room. The submission syncs to their Open Dental chart the moment they hit submit.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">A patient called but no one was available to answer. What happens?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Kasper can automatically send the patient an SMS letting them know their call was received and that someone will follow up. You can configure this missed-call automation in your settings so no inquiry slips through.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">How do I fill a last-minute cancellation?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Open Opportunity Finder, select the treatment type that fits the open slot, and Kasper pulls a ranked list of patients with matching unscheduled treatment — sorted by insurance benefits, treatment value, and appointment reliability. Call or text them directly from the interface with one click.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">A patient's auto-payment card was declined. What do I do?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Kasper flags it automatically in the Revenue Cycle Management dashboard and sends you a daily failed-payments report. You can retry the card from the dashboard or send the patient a text-to-pay link so they can update their payment method and pay immediately from their phone.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">The intraday dashboard shows color-coded flags — what do the colors mean?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">The dashboard uses color coding to highlight actionable items at a glance: overdue bills, incomplete paperwork, hygiene reminders due, and more. Red means act now before the patient leaves; yellow means review. Your onboarding specialist will walk you through the specific color scheme for your practice's configuration.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Can I use Kasper on my phone when away from the office?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes. The Kasper mobile app lets you answer calls, text patients, check the schedule, chat with the team, and receive real-time practice notifications from anywhere — useful for office managers and providers who are frequently away from the front desk.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">How do review requests work?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Kasper sends automated review request messages to patients after their appointments. You control the timing and message content. More reviews improve your practice's visibility in Google search results, helping new patients find you. You can also run one-time review campaigns to any segment of your patient list.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">What if something isn't working?</div>
        <div class="faq-a">Contact Kasper support at <a href="mailto:support@meetkasper.com">support@meetkasper.com</a> or call <a href="tel:8883128245">(888) 312-8245</a>. When you reach out, include the patient name or account if relevant, a description of what you expected vs. what happened, and a screenshot if possible — this gets your issue resolved faster.</div>
